-  default web security ineffective, all endpoints unauthenticated)**, affecting 4.0.0–4.0.5.
-  **This app does not meet its preconditions**: the CVE needs an app with *no custom Spring
-  Security configuration* that depends on `spring-boot-actuator-autoconfigure`. This app has an
-  explicit `SecurityConfig` and no actuator dependency. Not exploitable here — but it is the
-  reason to be on ≥ 4.0.6 rather than ahead of it.
-- `CVE-2026-40972` (DevTools remote-secret timing attack → RCE) applies only when
-  `spring.devtools.remote.secret` is set; it is not set here. `spring-boot-devtools` is
-  `optional`, so `spring-boot-maven-plugin` strips it from the repackaged jar.
-- **jjwt 0.12.6 → 0.13.0** is available. No advisory against 0.12.6; routine upgrade.
-- `springboot4-dotenv 5.1.0` is a small third-party library with a single maintainer. It reads
-  `.env` at startup only. Acceptable, but it is the one non-Spring, non-Postgres dependency in the
-  runtime path — worth pinning deliberately and reviewing on upgrade.
