-  the db run in `TZ` (default `Asia/Kuala_Lumpur`); leaving them on UTC would shift every
-  "working hours" deadline by 8 hours.
-- **Client IP.** `TRUST_FORWARDED_FOR=true` is set for the backend so rate limiting is per real
-  client. It is only safe because nginx *overwrites* `X-Forwarded-For` — keep it that way.
-- **HTTPS.** Served over plain http, `COOKIE_SECURE` must be `false` or the login cookie is
-  dropped. When nginx terminates TLS, set it to `true` and update `FRONTEND_BASE_URL` /
-  `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` to the https address.
-- **Health.** `/actuator/health/liveness` backs the compose healthcheck. nginx does not route
-  `/actuator`, so it isn't public.
-- **Shutdown.** `server.shutdown=graceful` lets in-flight requests finish on `docker compose stop`.
